WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.312
This is the executive briefing
for PKI and Certificates,

3
00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:07.787
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:07.787 --> 00:00:10.860
It's for the people who decide: the CIO,

5
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.162
the CISO, the PKI owner
and authorizing officials.

6
00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:16.587
The argument is short.

7
00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:21.331
Certificates prove who's who in every
other migration, and they keep working

8
00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:25.999
until the day they expire, so they fail
on their own clock, not the directory's.

9
00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:29.798
There's no single replacement for
the old certificate authority;

10
00:00:29.798 --> 00:00:32.963
the target is four issuers
and one lifecycle platform.

11
00:00:32.963 --> 00:00:37.712
And the move runs as its own program,
with the old authority retired last.

12
00:00:37.712 --> 00:00:42.087
Each decision slide names the decision,
its owner and when it's needed.

13
00:00:42.087 --> 00:00:43.390
Let's start with why.
